   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Logo Enter\n\nA stacked, overlapping group of round chips that spring in one by one, then hold. Ships with generic placeholder marks; set the chip count and colours to match your own.\n\nCategory: social. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A cluster of partner or integration marks should arrive together as an overlapping group.\n- A positioning or proof beat needs several marks to land stacked.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need a single product logo or wordmark lockup: use a logo sting or resolve kinetic text into the name.\n- The marks must orbit or scatter rather than stack on one axis.\n\nVariables:\n- count (number, 1-6): Chips, default 4\n- diameter (number, 48-300): Diameter, default 118\n- overlap (number, 0-150): Overlap, default 38\n- ring_color (color): Ring, default \"#ffffff\"\n- orientation (enum): Orientation, default \"horizontal\"\n- stagger (number, 0-30): Stagger, default 7\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Logo Enter\n\n  A stacked, overlapping group of round chips that spring in one by one, then hold. Ships with generic placeholder marks; set the chip count and colours to match your own.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/logo-enter/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"logo-enter\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\":\"count\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"content\",\"label\":\"Chips\",\"description\":\"How many chips (1 to 6). Each shows a generic placeholder mark.\",\"default\":4,\"min\":1,\"max\":6,\"step\":1},{\"id\":\"diameter\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Diameter\",\"description\":\"Chip diameter in pixels on a 1280x720 frame.\",\"default\":118,\"min\":48,\"max\":300,\"step\":1,\"unit\":\"px\"},{\"id\":\"overlap\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Overlap\",\"description\":\"How far each chip tucks under the previous one.\",\"default\":38,\"min\":0,\"max\":150,\"step\":1,\"unit\":\"px\"},{\"id\":\"ring_color\",\"type\":\"color\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Ring\",\"description\":\"Colour of the ring around each chip.\",\"default\":\"#ffffff\"},{\"id\":\"orientation\",\"type\":\"enum\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Orientation\",\"description\":\"Stack direction.\",\"default\":\"horizontal\",\"options\":[{\"value\":\"horizontal\",\"label\":\"Horizontal\"},{\"value\":\"vertical\",\"label\":\"Vertical\"}]},{\"id\":\"stagger\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"motion\",\"label\":\"Stagger\",\"description\":\"Frames between one chip and the next (30 fps).\",\"default\":7,\"min\":0,\"max\":30,\"step\":1,\"unit\":\"frames\"},{\"id\":\"speed\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"motion\",\"label\":\"Speed\",\"description\":\"Playback speed multiplier.\",\"default\":1,\"min\":0.25,\"max\":4,\"step\":0.05,\"unit\":\"x\"}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Logo Enter</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        .le-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        #le-scene { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        #le-row { display: flex; }\n        .le-chip { flex: none; border-radius: 50%; box-sizing: border-box; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; box-shadow: 0 20px 48px rgba(0,0,0,0.5); }\n        .le-mark { display: flex; }\n        .le-mark svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; }\n\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"logo-enter\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"le-clip\" class=\"le-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n<div id=\"le-scene\"><div id=\"le-row\"></div></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            // Frame-based helpers, written from their definitions.\n            var Easing = (function () {\n              function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n                return function (x) {\n                  if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                  if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                  var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                  for (var i = 0; i < 40; i++) {\n                    var u = 1 - t;\n                    var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                    if (Math.abs(cx - x) < 1e-6) break;\n                    if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                    t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                  }\n                  var v = 1 - t;\n                  return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n                };\n              }\n              return {\n                bezier: bezier,\n                linear: function (t) { return t; },\n                quad: function (t) { return t * t; },\n                cubic: function (t) { return t * t * t; },\n                sin: function (t) { return 1 - Math.cos((t * Math.PI) / 2); },\n                poly: function (n) { return function (t) { return Math.pow(t, n); }; },\n                ease: bezier(0.42, 0, 1, 1),\n                out: function (f) { return function (t) { return 1 - f(1 - t); }; },\n                inOut: function (f) { return function (t) { return t < 0.5 ? f(t * 2) / 2 : 1 - f((1 - t) * 2) / 2; }; }\n              };\n            })();\n            function interpolate(input, inR, outR, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var n = inR.length;\n              var left = o.extrapolateLeft || \"extend\";\n              var right = o.extrapolateRight || \"extend\";\n              var i = 1;\n              while (i < n - 1 && input > inR[i]) i++;\n              var a = inR[i - 1], b = inR[i];\n              if (input < inR[0] && left === \"clamp\") return outR[0];\n              if (input > inR[n - 1] && right === \"clamp\") return outR[n - 1];\n              var t = b === a ? 0 : (input - a) / (b - a);\n              if (o.easing) t = o.easing(t);\n              return outR[i - 1] + (outR[i] - outR[i - 1]) * t;\n            }\n            // Damped spring from rest to 1. durationInFrames stretches time so the spring has settled by then.\n            function spring(o) {\n              var c = o.config || {};\n              var mass = c.mass != null ? c.mass : 1;\n              var k = c.stiffness != null ? c.stiffness : 100;\n              var damp = c.damping != null ? c.damping : 10;\n              function at(t) {\n                var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / mass);\n                var z = damp / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * mass));\n                if (z < 1) {\n                  var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                  return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + ((z * w0) / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n                }\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              }\n              var t = Math.max(0, o.frame) / o.fps;\n              if (o.durationInFrames) {\n                var settle = 4, step = 1 / o.fps;\n                for (var s = settle; s > 0.05; s -= step) {\n                  if (Math.abs(1 - at(s)) > 0.001) { settle = s + step; break; }\n                  settle = s;\n                }\n                t = (Math.max(0, o.frame) / o.durationInFrames) * settle;\n                if (o.frame >= o.durationInFrames) return 1;\n              }\n              return at(t);\n            }\n            function parseColor(c) {\n              var m;\n              c = String(c).trim();\n              if ((m = /^#([0-9a-f]{3,8})$/i.exec(c))) {\n                var h = m[1];\n                if (h.length <= 4) h = h.split(\"\").map(function (x) { return x + x; }).join(\"\");\n                return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16), parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16), parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16), h.length === 8 ? parseInt(h.slice(6, 8), 16) / 255 : 1];\n              }\n              if ((m = /^rgba?\\(([^)]+)\\)/i.exec(c))) {\n                var p = m[1].split(\",\").map(Number);\n                return [p[0], p[1], p[2], p.length > 3 ? p[3] : 1];\n              }\n              return [0, 0, 0, 1];\n            }\n            function interpolateColors(t, inR, outR) {\n              var a = parseColor(outR[0]), b = parseColor(outR[1]);\n              var u = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (t - inR[0]) / (inR[1] - inR[0])));\n              return \"rgba(\" + [0, 1, 2].map(function (i) { return Math.round(a[i] + (b[i] - a[i]) * u); }).join(\",\") + \",\" + (a[3] + (b[3] - a[3]) * u) + \")\";\n            }\n            // Seeded 0..1 value: the same seed always gives the same number.\n            function random(seed) {\n              var s = String(seed), h = 2166136261;\n              for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n                h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\n                h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\n              }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 2246822519);\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 3266489917);\n              return ((h ^ (h >>> 15)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            // Fit a fixed-size design stage into the frame.\n            function fit(el, w, h, fill) {\n              var s = Math.min(root.clientWidth / w, root.clientHeight / h) * (fill || 1);\n              el.style.position = \"absolute\";\n              el.style.left = \"50%\";\n              el.style.top = \"50%\";\n              el.style.width = w + \"px\";\n              el.style.height = h + \"px\";\n              el.style.transform = \"translate(-50%, -50%) scale(\" + s + \")\";\n              return s;\n            }\n            // Drive draw(frame) from the timeline so seeking always draws the same picture.\n            function clockTween(tl, totalFrames, draw, rate) {\n              var clock = { frame: 0 };\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: totalFrames, duration: totalFrames / 30, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame * (rate || 1)); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n            var SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n            function svgEl(tag, attrs, parent) {\n              var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n              for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n              if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n              return e;\n            }\n\n\n                        // Stop-motion helpers: poses are held for `step` frames.\n            var DEFAULT_STEP = 3;\n            function qf(frame, step) { step = step || DEFAULT_STEP; return Math.floor(frame / step) * step; }\n            function qstep(frame, step) { step = step || DEFAULT_STEP; return Math.floor(frame / step); }\n            function hash01(seed) { return random(seed); }\n            function hashRange(seed, lo, hi) { return lo + hash01(seed) * (hi - lo); }\n            function paperJitter(frame, seed, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var amp = o.amp != null ? o.amp : 1.4, rotAmp = o.rotAmp != null ? o.rotAmp : 0.35;\n              var s = qstep(frame, o.step);\n              return { x: hashRange(seed + \":x:\" + s, -amp, amp), y: hashRange(seed + \":y:\" + s, -amp, amp), rot: hashRange(seed + \":r:\" + s, -rotAmp, rotAmp) };\n            }\n            function steppedRamp(frame, from, to, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var f = qf(frame, o.step);\n              if (f <= from) return 0;\n              if (f >= to) return 1;\n              var ease = o.ease || function (t) { return t; };\n              return ease((f - from) / (to - from));\n            }\n\n\n            function scaledStage(el, boost) {\n              var W = root.clientWidth, H = root.clientHeight;\n              var s = Math.min(W / 1280, H / 720) * (H > W ? (boost || 1.4) : 1);\n              el.style.position = \"absolute\"; el.style.left = \"0\"; el.style.top = \"0\";\n              el.style.width = W / s + \"px\"; el.style.height = H / s + \"px\";\n              el.style.transformOrigin = \"0 0\"; el.style.transform = \"scale(\" + s + \")\";\n              return s;\n            }\n\n            var scene = document.getElementById(\"le-scene\"), row = document.getElementById(\"le-row\");\n            scaledStage(scene, 1.6);\n            var count = Math.round(num(vars.count, 4, 1, 6));\n            var dia = num(vars.diameter, 118, 48, 300), overlap = num(vars.overlap, 38, 0, 150);\n            var ring = str(vars.ring_color, \"#ffffff\"), stagger = num(vars.stagger, 7, 0, 30), speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var vertical = pick(vars.orientation, [\"horizontal\", \"vertical\"], \"horizontal\") === \"vertical\";\n            row.style.flexDirection = vertical ? \"column\" : \"row\";\n            // Generic placeholder marks, none of them a real brand.\n            var MARKS = [\n              { bg: \"#F0EEE6\", svg: '<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path fill=\"#D9593B\" d=\"M12 1.5l2.6 7.1 7.4.5-5.8 4.7 1.9 7.2L12 17.1 5.9 21l1.9-7.2L2 9.1l7.4-.5z\"/></svg>' },\n              { bg: \"#0A0A0A\", svg: '<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"8.5\"/><path d=\"M8 12h8\"/></svg>' },\n              { bg: \"#0A0A0A\", svg: '<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"#fff\"><path d=\"M12 2.5l9 5.2v10.6l-9 5.2-9-5.2V7.7zm0 4.1L6.6 9.7v4.6l5.4 3.1 5.4-3.1V9.7z\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\"/></svg>' },\n              { bg: \"#0A0A0A\", svg: '<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"#fff\"><path d=\"M12 3l9.5 17h-19z\"/></svg>' },\n              { bg: \"#F0EEE6\", svg: '<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"#2b3a67\"><rect x=\"4\" y=\"4\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"5\"/></svg>' },\n              { bg: \"#0A0A0A\", svg: '<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"#fff\"><path d=\"M12 2l3 7 7 3-7 3-3 7-3-7-7-3 7-3z\"/></svg>' }\n            ];\n            var chips = [];\n            for (var i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n              var m = MARKS[i % MARKS.length];\n              var c = document.createElement(\"div\");\n              c.id = \"le-chip-\" + i; c.className = \"le-chip\";\n              c.style.width = c.style.height = dia + \"px\";\n              c.style.background = m.bg; c.style.border = \"5px solid \" + ring; c.style.zIndex = String(count - i);\n              if (i > 0) { if (vertical) c.style.marginTop = -overlap + \"px\"; else c.style.marginLeft = -overlap + \"px\"; }\n              var inner = document.createElement(\"div\");\n              inner.className = \"le-mark\"; inner.style.width = inner.style.height = dia * 0.52 + \"px\";\n              inner.innerHTML = m.svg; c.appendChild(inner);\n              row.appendChild(c); chips.push(c);\n            }\n            function draw(frame) {\n              chips.forEach(function (c, i) {\n                var s = spring({ fps: 30, frame: frame * speed - i * stagger, config: { damping: 13, stiffness: 130, mass: 0.8 } });\n                var sc = interpolate(s, [0, 1], [0.5, 1]), off = interpolate(s, [0, 1], [22, 0]);\n                c.style.opacity = s;\n                c.style.transform = (vertical ? \"translateX(\" + off + \"px)\" : \"translateY(\" + off + \"px)\") + \" scale(\" + sc + \")\";\n              });\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            clockTween(tl, 90, draw);\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"logo-enter\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
